IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sea-schooling`
IMPORT `sea-qa`

-- School Education Act 1999 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (sea-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role and
-- every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the two roles it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error. Each
-- question that takes a situation input is asked, for its own role, with the value under which the situation does not
-- hold (FALSE) and every later input ASSUMEd: the answer must be `does not arise for you`. Every situation input is a
-- BOOLEAN, so the trap of graffiti finding 31 (a CONSIDER ... OTHERWISE taking OTHERWISE for an ASSUMEd enumeration)
-- cannot hide a read of it.
--
-- For the parent (the baseline's seat), each case is asserted twice: once against a value worked by hand from the text
-- (most taken from the baseline's own cases, sea-cases-schooling.l4, with the lives' event ids), and once against the
-- baseline export's own answer on the same facts, carried into the layer's answer type. For the student and the
-- employer, the values are worked by hand from the text. Facts the lives do not state are HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked date` IS A DATE
ASSUME `unasked arrangements` IS A `My child's arrangements`
ASSUME `an unasked absence` IS A `My child's absence`
ASSUME `an unasked residence` IS A `My child's residence`
ASSUME `an unasked school` IS A `The school's offer`
ASSUME `an unasked option` IS AN Option
ASSUME `an unasked offence` IS AN Offence
ASSUME `an unasked referrer` IS A Referrer
ASSUME `an unasked ground` IS A Ground
ASSUME `an unasked step` IS A PanelStep
ASSUME `an unasked component` IS A Component
ASSUME `an unasked region` IS A Region
ASSUME `an unasked student offence` IS A `Student offence`

`as the parent` MEANS `I am the child's parent, or the adult responsible for the child`
`as the student` MEANS `I am the child or student`
`as the employer` MEANS `I employ a child, or would like to`

-- The baseline's fixtures (sea-cases-schooling.l4), with the same facts.
`enrolled at the local school` MEANS `My child's arrangements` WITH
    `enrolled at a school` IS TRUE
    `a parent is registered as home educator` IS FALSE
    `exempted by the Minister, conditions being complied with` IS FALSE
    `a section 11D notice is in force` IS FALSE
    `a section 11H notice of full-time employment is in force` IS FALSE
    `part-time employment with every section 11H(6) condition met` IS FALSE
