-- Must I ensure my child is enrolled and attends?
-- s 4: for ss 9(2) and 38(1) "parent" has only its day-to-day meaning.
#ASSERT `Must I ensure my child is enrolled and attends` `as the parent` TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Must I ensure my child is enrolled and attends` `as the parent` TRUE FALSE EQUALS (`yes if` (`Am I a parent who answers for enrolment and attendance` TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT `Must I ensure my child is enrolled and attends` `as the parent` FALSE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Must I ensure my child is enrolled and attends` `as the parent` FALSE TRUE EQUALS (`yes if` (`Am I a parent who answers for enrolment and attendance` FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT `Must I ensure my child is enrolled and attends` `as the student` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Must I ensure my child is enrolled and attends` `as the employer` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

